course: dictionary
lesson: 2159
title: Cornbread and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cornbread is a bread made from cornmeal, which is ground maize. You can learn a lot about a new word from the words around it, which are its context. «Tyrone helps Grandma make cornbread and feels useful» tells you cornbread is something you can help make in a kitchen.
explain: Look for clues in the phrases. «A slice of cornbread» shows it is cut into pieces like a loaf, and «skillet cornbread» and «cornbread muffins» show it can be baked in a pan or in small cake-shaped moulds. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: When context is not enough, a dictionary helps. Cornbread is a sweet or savoury bread, so the sentence does not have to tell you whether it tastes sweet or salty. Check the word in a dictionary to be sure of its meaning.
fact: Cornbread is made from cornmeal, which is ground maize.
fact: Cornbread can be sweet or savoury.
fact: It is often baked in a pan or skillet, and it is a traditional food of the southern United States.
fact: People often eat cornbread with chilli, barbecue, beans, and at Thanksgiving.
fact: The way of cooking maize that cornbread comes from was first used by Native Americans, and European settlers learned it from them.
exercise: What is cornbread made from? | *Cornmeal, which is ground maize | Potatoes and butter | Rice flour and eggs | Oats and honey
exercise: «Tyrone helps Grandma make cornbread and feels useful.» What does this sentence tell you about cornbread? | It is a sort of soup | It is a drink you pour from a jug | It is a game played outdoors | *It is something you can help make in a kitchen
exercise: Which country's traditional food is cornbread? | Australia | *The southern United States | Japan | Ireland
test: Cornbread is often baked in what? | A glass jar | A bath full of water | *A pan or skillet | A paper bag
test: Which phrase tells you cornbread can be shaped into small cakes? | Skillet cornbread | Thanksgiving dinner | *Cornbread muffins | A slice of cornbread
exam: «Cornbread is made from cornmeal, which is ground maize.» What does ground maize mean? | *Maize that has been crushed into a powder | A kind of bread that has no flour | Maize that is cooked and left whole | Maize that is grown under the sea
